>Is there any kind of "Player's Handbook" in existance which contains
>"hints and tips" about the numerous things you seem to be able to do? I

There is a Guidebook ("Guide to the Mazes of Menace" or something like
that). It should be included with Nethack, in the main directory as
Guidebook or guideboo.txt. But, for some reason, it was left out of (at
least) the 3.1.3 MS-DOS distribution. I'm not sure where it is available
for FTP. I _think_ it's on linc.cis.upenn.edu somewhere but I'm not
sure. Does anyone else remember?

Then there's the help accessed with the '?' key in the game.

>see words like "polymorph" and "polypile" in many message, and haven't a
>clue what they actually mean.

When you find a wand or ring of polymorph, you will...

Spoiler: [polypiling is putting lots of 'useless' things into a pile and
zapping a wand of polymorph at them.]

>1. People always seem to be talking about armour class. How do you find out
>   what your current AC actually is? It doesn't seem to be displayed anywhere.

It should be on the bottom line. 'AC: 10' means that your AC is 10 (the
worst one and the one many classes have at the beginning). Smaller ACs
are better.

>2. How do I put something into a sack? I can't find a command for it!

a)pply the sack (or bag)... Or drop it to the ground and #loot it.

>3. What are sinks for?

You can either q)uaff from them or k)ick (either the 'k' key or Ctrl-D,
depending on the number_pad option) them. Try it sometime and see what
happens...

>4. What are statues for (ie the "statue of an <xxx>" type objects?

Just a sort of decoration. Except that some wake up when you walk by
them... And you can hack them to pieces with a pick-axe or wand of
digging. Sometimes there's useful stuff inside.

One of the greatest features of Nethack is the endless exploration. Even
when you've played for many years, you still find new things to do every
once in a while. If you can't figure out what something does, try
something on it! (and if you die or get hurt, learn from the
experience...)

